   117	registered record (the pod reproduces the registered run). Each writes `gate/<cell>__<site>.json` with the comparison,
   118	round 1's own values, the binding (full-budget provenance, gate settings, input hashes, driver, dependency hashes), and
   119	the environment. The main run is refused unless both cells have a passing Mac record and a passing pod record from this
   120	machine's numerical stack, each with exactly the binding recomputed now. If
   121	the pod gate fails, the run stops and is reported; the frozen estimates stay primary.
   122	
   123	## 6. Cost and spending controls
   124	
   125	`python3 docs/revision/followup2/cost_estimate.py`: up to 29.48 core-hours, 3.18 USD at 0.108 USD per core-hour (19 cells x
   126	3 rounds priced as registered doubling checks plus a held-out evaluation each round); the gate cells run serially, 1.06
   127	hours; billed path 3.60 hours (gate, an X7-SC cell's three rounds with 16 workers starting the 9 X7-SC cells first, 0.3 h
   128	preparation and tail) = 2.01 USD at 0.56 USD per hour. Estimate 3.30 USD (x 1.25 = 4.12); **stop cap and reservation
   129	4.25 USD** in ledger category `followup` (cap 22 USD shared: reset 5, churn 8, Run A 3, Run B 4.25, total 20.25;
   130	`budget_followup.py reserve`). A paid run requires `--started-at <allocation time>`, a positive rate, and the launcher's attempts file
   131	(`--attempts`). Admission is checked before each gate cell and before every round of every
   132	cell, including its first, with the round's estimate plus its evaluation and a 0.1-hour shutdown allowance; a running round
   133	is never killed (author's instruction). A cell refused admission, or stopped by it after a completed round, keeps its frozen estimate as primary and is
   134	reported "stopped at the cost cap"; any partial result is kept under `partial` and never substituted; after the last running round finishes, the pod is deleted and verified. This is an admission limit, not a
   135	billing ceiling.
   136	
   137	**Launcher handoff (draft 5).** The launcher copy pushes to the pod, before every paid driver call, its current
   138	`<name>.attempts` file and the ledger, and passes `--attempts`, `--ledger`, `--run-tag`, `--started-at` (the current pod's
   139	allocation time), `--usd-per-hour` (the price ceiling MAXCPH), `--stop-file /root/STOP`, and `--soft-deadline` (its soft
   140	deadline). The driver reads the launcher's own event lines (`<pod> <epoch> start`, `<pod> <epoch> deleted`;
   141	`guards.attempts_spend`): each closed attempt counts at the ceiling, the open start is the current pod (counted from
   142	`--started-at`), and malformed or unordered lines are refused (tests with lines in the launcher's exact format); spend of
   143	earlier launches comes from the ledger rows tagged with the run tag, since the launcher truncates its file per launch. The
   144	driver checks the STOP file and the soft deadline before each gate cell and before every round of every cell, so it
   145	honours the launcher's between-stage stop without a mid-round stop (test).
   146	
   147	**Admission before every paid step (draft 6).** Before the pod's first paid step, and before each later one (the reset
   148	reproduction gate included), the launcher runs `python3 docs/revision/followup2/guards.py admit --cap-usd 4.25
   149	--usd-per-hour <ceiling> --started-at <allocation> --attempts <file> --ledger <ledger> --run-tag convergence --hours <step estimate>
   150	--stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline <soft>` and starts the step only on exit 0. Reservation: `budget_followup.py
   151	reserve convergence-<n> 3.40` grants 4.25 USD. The launcher copy itself (a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh`) is not part
   152	of this folder and is to be written and tested offline before allocation.
   153	
   154	**Launcher and the cap.** The pod launcher is a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh` with `results/pods/podctl.py`. Its soft
   155	deadline is the cap at the price ceiling MAXCPH, counted from the first creation request of the launch, so it holds across
   156	attempts; at the soft deadline the remote script stops before its next stage (a STOP file read between stages), and the
   157	driver's own admission check (`--cap-usd`, `--started-at`, `--attempts`) stops between stages or rounds as well. A running
   158	stage is never stopped (the author: do not kill jobs). The single exception is the watchdog, which deletes the pod at 1.3 x
   159	the cap at the price ceiling; that is the only mid-stage stop. Closed attempts are listed in the launcher's
   160	`<name>.attempts` file (event lines `<pod> <epoch> start` and `<pod> <epoch> deleted`), which the driver reads
   161	(`guards.attempts_spend`) and counts toward the
   162	cap before each paid attempt; a paid run without it is refused (no default of zero); after the launch the spend is recorded
   163	in the ledger (`budget_v2.py --record`).
   164	
   165	## 7. Steps
   166	
   167	1. Internal review to consensus; freeze the plan; save the Mac gate evidence.
   168	2. Reserve 4.25 USD in the ledger; one pod: the gate with `--site pod`, then `convergence_v2.py --workers 16 --evidence
   169	   <four gate records> --cap-usd 4.25 --started-at T --attempts A --ledger L --run-tag convergence --stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline S`; delete and verify; record the spend.
   170	3. Analysis on the Mac; a paper sentence and table, exploratory, after review.
