     1	claude-fable-5-2
     2	
     3	**→ Ambition.** The outside check this paper most needs is an honest-churn arm (honest providers also replace identities), because the main findings depend on its absence; see problem 4.
     4	
     5	## 1. Files read
     6	
     7	I could not run code: the session blocked Python. All recomputation below is hand arithmetic on values in the files.
     8	
     9	- **Read in full:** `main.pdf` (29 pages), `protocol-v2.yaml`, `predictions-v2.md`, `addendum.md`, `stability-result.json`, `audit.json`, `scoring.json`, `operations-ledger.md`, `h4-family.py`, `h4-containment.md`.
    10	- **Read in part:** `revision-program-design.md` (sections 3 to 9 only).
    11	- **Read in part:** `report.md` (lines 1 to 40 in full; lines 163 to 302 cut at 400 characters; Q2 per-market lines 41 to 162 not read).
    12	- **Read in part:** `eligibility.json` (flag list and tallies only), `posthoc.json` (Q1 split and lottery blocks only).
    13	- **Read in part:** `lottery_seeds.csv` and `lottery_train.csv` (header, first rows, row counts).
    14	- **Outline only:** `score_v2.py`, `test_scoring.py`, `audit_v2.py`, `posthoc_v2.py` (function names and assert lines). I make no claim about their logic.
    15	- No file failed to open.
    16	
    17	## 2. Summary verdict
    18	
    19	The paper is honest and its numbers match its outputs. Its conclusions are narrower than its framing. The main result is a null: R3 and a history-based comparator differ by 0.021 in attacker gain. The "equivalent" label comes from a wide margin, and three things can change it: search error as large as the margin, variation between markets, and a comparator that was not selected on gain. The two Q1 "families" are mostly one test. The model has no honest churn, so identity age labels the attacker almost perfectly. The theory is correct but thin. The paper reads as an audit record, not as a finding.
    20	
    21	Scores: **WEIS 2/5, AAMAS 2/5, EC 1/5** (details in section 8).
    22	
    23	## 3. Claims
    24	
    25	| # | Claim | Evidence | Verdict |
    26	|---|---|---|---|
    27	| 1 | Under uniform audits with free replacement, a ban costs nothing | Corollary 1, proof sketch | **Narrower.** True if rivals are honest and do not react, re-entry loses no round, and the rule keeps no identity memory. B2's memory is not checkable. |
    28	| 2 | R3 and C* are equivalent within ±0.05, R3 lower, under two attack families | Report Q1 lines 9 to 18 | **Narrower.** The point estimates reproduce. "Equivalent" depends on the margin, and "two families" is mostly one (problems 1, 2). |
    29	| 3 | Priority phase and newest-first targeting are substitutes | Report line 32 | **Supported** for the prescribed searches. The direct reading is stronger: the priority phase adds −0.001 once newest-first targeting is on. |
    30	| 4 | B3 to R3 gain reduction replicates on 3 of 6 fresh markets | Report lines 23 to 29, `audit.json` | **Supported as stated.** |
    31	| 5 | Welfare attacks and mixtures lower efficiency to 0.84 and 0.92 to 0.95 | Report lines 170 to 181, `posthoc.json` | **Narrower.** The 0.84 result is solid. The mixture result is arithmetic on two existing points, and the W1 search returned the null policy (problem 8). |
    32	
    33	## 4. Correctness checks
    34	
    35	| Item | Paper | My value | Source |
    36	|---|---|---|---|
    37	| Q1 pooled d, D2+H3 | 0.021 | **0.0207, reproduced** | Mean of six per-market values, report lines 13 to 18 |
    38	| Q1 pooled d, X7-SC | 0.024 | **0.0243, reproduced** | Same lines |
    39	| Q1 mean gains (C*, R3) | 0.086, 0.065; 0.091, 0.067 | **0.0856, 0.0649; 0.0913, 0.0670, reproduced** | `stability-result.json`, `mean_old` |
    40	| Q1 category, p-values | equivalent, R3 lower; 0.0004, 0.0008 | **Reproduced** (0.0002 / 0.5; times 2) | `audit.json` q1 |
    41	| Q1 doubled-search d | 0.030, 0.024 | **0.0295, 0.0243, reproduced** | Paper Table 5 columns |
    42	| Q2 contrasts | P −0.083, G −0.095, S 0.004, PG 0.082, G given P=0 −0.177, G given P=1 −0.014 | **Reproduced**; conditional effects average to the main effects | Report line 32 |
    43	| Q4 gain differences | 0.041, 0.469, 0.057, 0.263, 0.183, 0.027 | **Reproduced** to 4 decimals | `stability-result.json`, F000 minus F111 |
    44	| Q4 passing count | 3 of 6 | **3, reproduced**; Holm 0.0004 × 6 = 0.0024 | `audit.json` q4 |
    45	| Welfare efficiency | 0.839, 0.840, 0.840; W1 0.997 | **Reproduced** | Report lines 170 to 181 |
