     1	# Reset experiment: plan (draft 5, 2026-11-10; draft 4 had internal consensus and the author's approval, cap 10 USD; no spend yet)
     2	
     3	**Why.** The round-9 fresh reviewer (problem 2, `docs/paper/external-review-r9.md`): the gain is excess profit when
     4	identity replacement is available; it does not show how much of that profit comes from the ability to replace an
     5	identity. This plan measures that, within the searched D2 family, on the second test's markets.
     6	
     7	**Draft 5** (2026-11-10) applies the Fable 5.2 driver review (`docs/revision/roster/fable52-reset-driver-r1.md`, triage
     8	`docs/paper/fable52-triage.md`): a reproduction criterion that a cross-platform run can meet, a pod gate, the driver's
     9	location under `docs/`, the diagnostics built and run free before the pod, a doubling ground truth, and clarified scoring.
    10	It needs one internal review round.
    11	
    12	**Status.** Draft 4 applied the round-3 caveats (`docs/revision/roster/{sol,astra}-reset-plan-r{1,2,3}.md`; round 3: both accept-with-caveat).
    13	After consensus: a decision card for the author. Nothing runs before the author approves the spend. This file is frozen
    14	(commit hash in the operations ledger) before any paid cell starts.
    15	
    16	## 1. What already exists (free; seen before this plan)
    17	
    18	The D2+H3 family is D2 plus one binary knob `x` (`sim/policies/identity.py`: `x = 1` exits in the round after a failed
    19	audit and re-enters under a fresh identity; `x = 0` is plain D2). Design 8.1 listed D2 on all seven markets ("Matched core
    20	extras"); budget cut 3 removed the fresh-market D2 cells, so D2 was run at the headline market only. At `headline@rho0.2`,
    21	same 200 evaluation seeds, same frozen reference per rule (checked: `seeds` and reference `upstream` hashes equal):
    22	
    23	| Rule | g(D2+H3) | g(D2) | I = g(D2+H3) - g(D2) | Paired SE of I | D2+H3 doubling check |
    24	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
    25	| B2 | 0.5851 | 0.0027 | 0.5824 | 0.0011 | not scheduled |
    26	| B3 (F000) | 0.3502 | 0.0435 | 0.3067 | 0.0012 | flagged |
    27	| R3 (F111) | 0.0486 | 0.0361 | 0.0124 | 0.0009 | flagged |
    28	| C* | 0.0872 | 0.0433 | 0.0439 | 0.0008 | not flagged |
    29	
    30	Source: `results/v2/eval/all/evaluate/headline@rho0.2__{rule}__{D2+H3,D2}__profit.json`, field `gain`; flags from
    31	`report.json` `search_flagged`; the D2 cells had no scheduled doubling check. At `headline@rho1`, R3 and C* are in the
    32	terminal-reserve collapse and I is 0.0025.
    33	
    34	Reading, exploratory: at the headline market the D2+H3 search leaves about 0.31 more gain than the D2 search against B3,
    35	and about 0.01 against R3; the B3 - R3 gap is 0.302 under D2+H3 and 0.007 under D2.
    36	
    37	## 2. Estimand
    38	
    39	For rule r in {B3 (F000), R3 (F111), C*} and fresh market m:
    40	
    41	I(r, m) = mean over the 200 evaluation seeds of g(D2+H3 winner) - g(D2 winner),
    42	
    43	both against the same frozen truthful reference of (r, m), so the reference term cancels. **I is a difference between two
    44	prescribed finite searches over nested families (D2 within D2+H3), not an identified optimal value of replacement and not
    45	a system-wide prohibition of replacement.** The two searches differ in dimension, Sobol starts, and corner sets (D2 128,
    46	D2+H3 256 corner vectors), with the same restart and evaluation budgets; the two winners can differ in every knob, not
    47	only `x`. A negative I can come from search error. The fixed-policy diagnostic in section 4 separates the switch from
    48	re-optimisation.
    49	
    50	## 3. Cells and execution contract
    51	
    52	- **New search cells.** D2 x {F000, F111, C*} x fresh0..fresh5 at rho 0.2: 18 cells, exactly the design-8.1 cells that cut
    53	  3 removed, with their registered settings (D2 knob space and budget, the market's training seeds for search, its 200
    54	  evaluation seeds), each with a doubling check (design 6.5, held-out evaluation of the doubled winner on the same seeds).
    55	- **Driver.** A separate follow-up script (`docs/revision/followup/reset_followup_v2.py`, under `docs/` because the code
    56	  freeze allows changes only there; written and tested before any spend) that
    57	  imports the frozen stage functions of `scripts/revision_v2.py` at the protocol-v2 tag (`job`, `stage_search`, the
    58	  evaluation and doubling stages) and builds the 18 jobs from the uncut cell list. It bypasses only three things, each
    59	  recorded as a deviation: the fixed manifest path and cut list (`sim/manifest_v2.py` `effective`), the hard-coded doubling
    60	  eligibility (`doublings`), and the original freeze. It writes to a new directory (`results/v2/followup-reset/`) and
    61	  never writes to `results/v2/eval/all`.
    62	- **Inputs the frozen stages read.** The search, evaluation, and doubling stages read their dependencies from the output
    63	  directory (`menu()`, `reference_of()`, `select_reference()`). Before any episode, the driver copies into the new
    64	  directory, read-only, every record those stages read for the 18 cells: the frozen reference records, the search
    65	  records and bank-source records that build each (context, rule) menu, and the original cuts-3 bank membership. It
    66	  takes the list from the `upstream` fields of the existing records and checks each copy's SHA-256 against them; it
    67	  refuses on any missing record or mismatch.
    68	- **Two freezes.** A pre-evaluation freeze after the 18 searches: selected policies, references, configurations, seeds,
    69	  and search records, with their hashes (the frozen evaluation stage requires it). Evaluation and doubling then run
    70	  against that freeze, and a final inventory lists every output record with its hash. The inventory is written after
    71	  the outputs, so no record hashes itself.
    72	- **Freeze validator.** The frozen `run()` calls `accept()`, which requires the original manifest's full record set, so it
    73	  cannot admit the 18 restored cells. The driver therefore has its own acceptance check, run before evaluation and before
    74	  doubling: every record of the follow-up dependency set (the copied inputs, the 18 search records, the pre-evaluation
    75	  freeze) exists and matches its hash; the identity-salt hash matches; each new job's configuration hash equals the
    76	  recorded container hash. Copied records keep their original provenance, including their recorded configuration
    77	  hashes. Tests: it refuses a missing freeze, a changed selected-policy record, a changed salt, and a changed copied input.
    78	- **References in doubling.** The held-out gain of a doubled winner uses the unchanged frozen reference. Any reference
    79	  reselection the doubling stage computes is recorded as a diagnostic only.
    80	- **References.** The existing frozen reference records are read, not re-selected; the driver refuses to start if any
    81	  reference file's SHA-256 differs from the hash in the original records' `upstream`.
    82	- **Configurations.** Linux pods from the same image as the evaluation; before any episode the driver checks that each
    83	  fresh market's configuration hash equals the recorded container hash (`addendum.json` `deviations.configs`), so the
    84	  new cells use the same configurations as the D2+H3 records they are paired with (the recorded 1-ulp deviation stays as
    85	  it is).
    86	- **Pairing and code checks (draft 5).** Before any episode the driver refuses a job whose runner, salt, configuration,
    87	  root, seeds, rule parameters, or context differ from its frozen reference's provenance; an unknown commit; a runner or
    88	  `sim/` that differs from protocol-v2; an output inside `--src` or `eval/all`; and a salt mismatch. The inventory records
    89	  Python, numpy, machine, platform, and the driver's hash.
    90	- **Validation before spend (free, on the Mac).** (a) Reproduction of the registered `headline@rho0.2|F111|D2` search and
    91	  evaluation. Draft 4 required identical knobs and per-seed gains. Measured on 2026-11-09/10: a Mac arm64 run and a Linux
    92	  amd64 container run both match on configuration, salt, runner, budget, rule parameters, episode count (15,660), archive
    93	  sizes, and the twin result, with selected knobs equal to 2.6e-13 relative and per-seed gains to 2.0e-14; evaluating the
    94	  registered knobs on the Mac gives per-seed gains within 5e-17 of the record (102 of 200 seeds bit-identical). The
    95	  evaluation of fixed knobs is not always this close: one of the 128 corner controls of the Mac rerun differs by 1.5e-5
    96	  with identical knobs (the other 127 within 2e-18), consistent with a near-tie flipping a discrete branch in an episode;
    97	  in the Linux container all 128 controls are bit-identical to the record. The drift source is therefore not isolated to
    98	  the optimiser. Last-bit
    99	  arithmetic differences grow through the search; these runs did not reproduce bit identity across platforms, and the
   100	  draft-4 rule is replaced as a recorded deviation. **Draft-5 criterion** (`compare()`). Exact: the provenance keys runner, salt, configuration, rule
   101	  parameters, root, training, validation and evaluation seeds, context and budget (the commit may differ); the episode
   102	  count; the attack and twin archive sizes; `best_source`; the discrete knobs; the search and evaluation dependency ids;
   103	  the reference hash; the control set (knobs in order). Within 1e-9: the twin's best value. Reported, not gated: the
   104	  corner controls' objective values (count and largest difference), because a near-tie in a non-selected corner policy
   105	  can flip a discrete branch. Finite: the knobs, the attack, twin and control objective values, and the per-seed gains. Tolerance: continuous knobs within 1e-9 relative and per-seed
   106	  gains within 1e-9 absolute (about 10^4 times the drift measured, and far below the paired standard error of about
   107	  0.0009). The Mac runs pass this criterion. **Pod gate:** the pod first reruns the same reproduction (about 0.34 USD of
   108	  billed time: 2,084 s search plus evaluation at 0.56 USD per hour); the author decided (card `touchstone-reset-repro-pass`,
   109	  2026-11-10) that the 18 cells start only if the pod's reproduction is bit-identical (`--reproduce --require-identical`);
   110	  any difference stops the pod and is reported. The draft-5 criterion applies to the Mac validations (`identical` requires bit-equal knobs, gains, twin value,
   111	  attack objective and every control value). The reproduction path runs every pre-episode check
   112	  (salt, commit, code, pairing, configuration) before its search and saves `gate.json` and an inventory with the
   113	  environment (Python, numpy with BLAS and LAPACK, SciPy, CMA, CPU). (b) An
   114	  integration test runs the complete path (input copies, search, pre-evaluation freeze, evaluation, doubling, inventory)
   115	  for one fresh-market cell at smoke size, including the driver's acceptance check, which proves every dependency
   116	  resolves (passed, 2026-11-09). (d) Doubling ground truth: the driver's doubling stage reruns the registered doubling
   117	  check of `fresh0@rho0.2|F111|D2+H3|profit` on the Mac (`--reproduce-doubling`), after the full preflight, saving a record with provenance and dependency
   118	  hashes, `gate.json`, and an inventory; compared by `compare_doubling()`: required fields present; finite values; exact on
   119	  the flag, the seeds and the discrete knobs; 1e-9 on the continuous held-out knobs, the attack and reference
   120	  changes, and the held-out per-seed gains. The saved result must pass before any pod is created. (c) Unit tests: the driver refuses a
   121	  changed reference hash, a missing input record, a wrong configuration hash, and an output directory inside `eval/all`.
   122	
   123	## 4. Diagnostics (evaluation only, no search)
   124	
   125	For three rules on seven markets: the base and doubled D2+H3 winners (42 policies) and the base D2 winners (21; the doubled
   126	D2 winners are not included), on the 200 evaluation seeds, re-run with reset and ban instrumentation (63 single-policy
   127	evaluations; the existing gain records carry no reset counts, so none is reused); the selected `x`; per episode the number of resets, the probability of at least one reset, the rounds of resets,
   128	and the rounds spent banned. Check that every D2 winner has zero resets. **Reverse switch (draft 5):** each of the 18 D2 winners re-evaluated with
   129	`x = 1` and every other knob unchanged (18 more evaluations). The diagnostics are built and tested in the driver (`diagnostics`
   130	stage) before any pod. Order: the instrumentation is validated on the registered headline cells before the pod; the
   131	diagnostics of the 18 new D2 winners and their reverse switches run on the Mac after the pod's records are retrieved.
   132	Construction: a D2 winner is embedded in D2+H3 by adding `x` (0 for itself, 1 for the reverse switch); each switch is
   133	the mean difference of normalised profits on the evaluation seeds, the reference cancelling. Resets are the focal
   134	provider's identities of generation 1 or more; ban rounds are the ban lengths imposed on its identities; rounds without
   135	an offer are counted separately. Saved per policy: the seed identifiers, the per-seed normalised profits, the per-seed switch differences, and the
   136	reset and ban counts per episode; a D2 winner with any reset stops the run. Spot check: `fresh0@rho0.2|F111` is also
   137	diagnosed on the pod (`--diag-cells`); the Mac's reset and ban counts must equal the pod's exactly, and its numerical
   138	values must
   139	meet the draft-5 tolerance against it. **Fixed-policy switch:** each of the 42 D2+H3
   140	winners re-evaluated with `x` set to 0 and every other knob unchanged (42 more; a winner that already has `x = 0` is
   141	reported as identical and not re-run); g(winner) - g(winner, x = 0) is the effect of the switch
   142	without re-optimisation, reported beside I.
   143	
   144	## 5. Analysis (fixed now)
   145	
   146	- **Intervals.** Per market: paired seed bootstrap (9,999 resamples, percentile, 95%), the same resampled seed indices for
   147	  every rule and family of that market, so contrasts across rules stay paired. Pooled: equal market weights; in each
   148	  replicate, seeds are resampled independently within each market and the pooled statistic is the mean of the six market
   149	  means; percentile interval. Nominal and descriptive; conditional on the six markets and the frozen policies and
   150	  references.
   151	- **Statistics.** I(r, m) and pooled I(r); the contrasts I(B3) - I(R3) and I(C*) - I(R3); the absolute gaps
   152	  G(D2+H3) = g_B3 - g_R3 under D2+H3 and G(D2) under D2, pooled.
   153	- **Share.** S = 1 - pooled G(D2) / pooled G(D2+H3), a ratio of pooled contrasts, computed in every bootstrap replicate.
   154	  S is reported only if the lower bound of pooled G(D2+H3) exceeds 0.05; otherwise "not defined". No clipping; S can be
   155	  negative or above 1. The absolute gaps are always reported beside it.
   156	- **Market sensitivity (draft 5).** The sign count of I(B3) - I(R3) and I(C*) - I(R3) over the six markets, and S with
   157	  each market left out in turn (six values), each with its own five-market denominator gate (lower bound of the
   158	  five-market pooled G(D2+H3) above 0.05; otherwise that value is "not defined"), for the base and the doubled results
   159	  separately. A nested best-of sensitivity (the better of the D2 and D2+H3 winners per cell) is deferred: it is not
   160	  part of this plan.
   161	- **Doubling flags.** For each D2 cell, the attack change and the reference-reselection change of its doubling check are
   162	  reported separately.
   163	- **Doubled versions** of the same statistics, as in the paper's `tab:ph-doubled`. The base (frozen) searches are primary,
   164	  as in the paper; the doubled versions are reported beside them.
   165	- No confirmatory test, no multiplicity family, no change to any registered decision.
   166	
   167	## 6. Pre-specified expectations and labels
   168	
   169	Written before any fresh D2 result exists. **The six markets, their seeds, and their D2+H3 outcomes were already observed;
   170	only the D2 outcomes are unseen.** This is a descriptive follow-up specified on 2026-11-09 after the round-9 review and
   171	after the headline contrast was seen, not an independent replication.
   172	
   173	Expectations: on all six fresh markets (each market counted; a single market against it fails the expectation), I(B3) > I(R3) and I(C*) > I(R3); pooled S defined and greater than 0.5. Expectations are
   174	scored on point estimates (this is a descriptive follow-up; "met" does not mean that an interval excludes the threshold),
   175	with the denominator gate of section 5 applied separately to the base and the doubled results. Each expectation is
   176	scored as met, failed, or not established: **met** if it holds under both the base and the doubled searches; **failed** if
   177	it fails under both; **not established (search-sensitive)** if the two disagree. An undefined S and a missing cell are
   178	reported as such, separately from failures. A failure is not read as evidence for any particular cause (search error and
   179	mixed outcomes are possible). Only if the pooled-S expectation is met may the paper say: within the D2 family, at the
   180	fixed parameters and search budgets, most of the estimated B3 - R3 gap under the prescribed searches disappears when the
   181	attacker cannot replace its identity.
   182	
   183	## 7. Cost
   184	
   185	**Work.** Measured benchmark (`experiments/v2/benchmark/timings.json`): one unit = a headline D2+H3 cell, 0.579
   186	core-hours. Per D2 cell: 1 unit + 160 further seeds (0.046) + doubling with held-out evaluation (0.479); 18 cells = 27.45
   187	units. Diagnostics: 63 instrumented evaluations + up to 42 switch evaluations = up to 105 single-policy evaluations of
   188	200 episodes, priced conservatively at the profit-evaluation stage's cost for 200 seeds (0.058 units each, although that
   189	stage evaluates more than one profile) = about 6.1 units. Total about 33.6 units = **about 19.4 core-hours**. Draft 5
   190	moves the diagnostics to the Mac (free) and adds the pod gate (about 0.34 USD); the pod estimate below is kept as an
   191	upper bound.
   192	
   193	**Billed pod time.** One 16-vCPU pod at the recorded 0.56 USD per hour; searches with 16 workers, evaluation, doubling,
   194	and diagnostics with at most 10 (operations ledger). Stage schedule with incomplete worker batches and equal benchmark
   195	task times: searches, evaluation, and doubling about 1.77 hours (internal review's computation); diagnostics about 0.6
   196	hours (105 evaluations in batches of 10); preparation 0.3 hours; idle tail 0.3 hours = **about 3.0 billed hours, about
   197	1.66 USD**. The benchmark's unit price (0.0625 USD per unit, at its 0.108 USD per core-hour) gives about 2.10 USD; the plan
   198	uses the larger.
   199	
   200	| Item | Estimate | Cap |
   201	|---|---:|---:|
   202	| Option A: 18 D2 cells, doubling checks, diagnostics | 1.66 to 2.10 USD | **10.00 USD** (author, 2026-11-09) |
   203	
   204	A failed attempt counts toward the cap; the cap leaves room for one early failure, not for a full second run. Option B (an X7-SC variant with replacement disabled) is dropped from this plan: its
   205	constrained family, incumbents, and corner controls would need their own specification (the frozen X7-SC search inserts
   206	D2+H3 incumbents that can replace), so it is not offered for approval.
   207	
   208	**Budget.** `docs/revision/budget-ledger.json`: spent 50.869 USD of the 55 USD approval limit. The author approved option A
   209	on the board on 2026-11-09 and set the cap to 10 USD ("make the cap $10 to ensure we're not blocked by a low cap"). The
   210	ledger needs a new category `followup` with cap 10.00 and the approval limit raised to 61 USD (50.869 + 10 = 60.869,
   211	`python3 -c "print(50.869+10)"`). `scripts/budget_v2.py` is frozen, so the tested wrapper
   212	`docs/revision/followup/budget_followup.py --approve 61 10 TEXT` records both, refuses a limit below spend plus the cap,
   213	and keeps the earlier approval text. The estimate is unchanged (1.66 to 2.10 USD); the higher cap only prevents a stop from a low
   214	cap. Stop at the cap.
   215	
   216	## 8. Steps
   217	
   218	1. Internal review of this plan to consensus; freeze it (commit).
   219	2. Decision card: approved on 2026-11-09, cap 10 USD (card `touchstone-reset-spend`).
   220	3. On approval: write and test the driver (TDD); on the Mac (free), validations (a), (b) and (d) must pass through the
   221	   corrected paths (preflight run, record with provenance and dependency hashes, `gate.json` and an inventory saved in a
   222	   new directory each: `results/v2/followup-repro-v2`, `results/v2/followup-repro-doubling-v2`); earlier passes on the
   223	   older path do not count and the diagnostics are validated on the registered headline
   224	   cells, all before any pod is created.
   225	4. One pod: the reproduction gate first (bit identity, `--require-identical`; stop and report on any difference), then `--stage all` with
   226	   `--diag-cells fresh0@rho0.2|F111|D2|profit` (inputs, search, freeze, evaluate, doubling, spot diagnostics, inventory);
   227	   records retrieved, the pod deleted and the deletion verified, the spend recorded.
   228	   Launcher rule (launcher review r11): an ambiguous creation answer ends the launch with no further request; the watchdog
   229	   deletes any late pod and settles for 30 minutes. After any launch that ends AMBIGUOUS or UNRESOLVED BILLING, check the
   230	   Runpod console for pods named ts-r-TAG the next day, record the final spend bound from `watchdog.log`, and relaunch
   231	   only after that check.
   232	5. On the Mac after retrieval: the diagnostics of all 18 D2 winners and their reverse switches (`--stage diagnostics`),
   233	   checked against the pod's spot-check cell. The three headline cells (registered D2 records) run on the Mac before the
   234	   pod (`--headline-diagnostics`, 200 seeds); with the 18 fresh cells this gives the 63 policies and 42 switch
   235	   comparisons of section 4 plus the 21 reverse switches.
   236	6. Analysis: a new `reset` block in `posthoc_v2.py` (tested first), a table, and a paragraph in section 9 with sites; the
   237	   section-1 headline numbers enter at the same time, labelled exploratory.
   238	7. Internal review of the paper change, then the next external package.

