   145	honours the launcher's between-stage stop without a mid-round stop (test).
   146	
   147	**Admission before every paid step (draft 6).** Before the pod's first paid step, and before each later one (the reset
   148	reproduction gate included), the launcher runs `python3 docs/revision/followup2/guards.py admit --cap-usd 4.25
   149	--usd-per-hour <ceiling> --started-at <allocation> --attempts <file> --ledger <ledger> --run-tag convergence --hours <step estimate>
   150	--stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline <soft>` and starts the step only on exit 0. Reservation: `budget_followup.py
   151	reserve convergence-<n> 3.40` grants 4.25 USD. The launcher copy itself (a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh`) is not part
   152	of this folder and is to be written and tested offline before allocation.
   153	
   154	**Launcher and the cap.** The pod launcher is a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh` with `results/pods/podctl.py`. Its soft
   155	deadline is the cap at the price ceiling MAXCPH, counted from the first creation request of the launch, so it holds across
   156	attempts; at the soft deadline the remote script stops before its next stage (a STOP file read between stages), and the
   157	driver's own admission check (`--cap-usd`, `--started-at`, `--attempts`) stops between stages or rounds as well. A running
   158	stage is never stopped (the author: do not kill jobs). The single exception is the watchdog, which deletes the pod at 1.3 x
   159	the cap at the price ceiling; that is the only mid-stage stop. Closed attempts are listed in the launcher's
   160	`<name>.attempts` file (event lines `<pod> <epoch> start` and `<pod> <epoch> deleted`), which the driver reads
   161	(`guards.attempts_spend`) and counts toward the
   162	cap before each paid attempt; a paid run without it is refused (no default of zero); after the launch the spend is recorded
   163	in the ledger (`budget_v2.py --record`).
   164	
   165	## 7. Steps
   166	
   167	1. Internal review to consensus; freeze the plan; save the Mac gate evidence.
   168	2. Reserve 4.25 USD in the ledger; one pod: the gate with `--site pod`, then `convergence_v2.py --workers 16 --evidence
   169	   <four gate records> --cap-usd 4.25 --started-at T --attempts A --ledger L --run-tag convergence --stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline S`; delete and verify; record the spend.
   170	3. Analysis on the Mac; a paper sentence and table, exploratory, after review.
